BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 600.6 Tm (Task 2 model answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 581.7 Tm (Whether students or the state should pay for university is a question on which people feel strongly.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 565.8 Tm (Both views have merit, but I believe that university should be free, or very nearly so.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 540.8 Tm (Those who want students to pay argue that graduates usually earn more than other workers, so it) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 524.9 Tm (is fair that they cover the cost of the education that brings them this advantage. They also point out) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 508.9 Tm (that free education must be paid for by taxes, including the taxes of people who never went to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 493.0 Tm (university.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 468.0 Tm (On the other hand, free university gives every talented young person the same chance, whatever) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 452.1 Tm (their familyís income. When fees are high, many able students from poorer homes decide not to) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 436.1 Tm (apply, and the country loses their skills. A well-educated population also benefits everyone,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 420.2 Tm (through better doctors, engineers and teachers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 395.2 Tm (In conclusion, although the argument that graduates should pay has some force, I am convinced) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 56.0 379.3 Tm (that the wider benefits of free university education outweigh its cost.) Tj ET
